    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d433">

                <pb facs="0548" n="538" sameAs="frus:frus1948v07/pg538"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.93/11–348: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Mukden</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Ward</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi><anchor n="30" xml:id="d433-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mukden</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-11-03T11:00:00+08:00">November 3,
                            1948—11 a. m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received November 3—2:36 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>494. Not unlikely I shall be taken to task by local authorities over Government
                    bombing Mukden in as much bombers and presumably bombs were obtained by
                    Government from United States, and shall, therefore, appreciate being informed
                    soonest if we made appeal to Government cease bombing. Such information, if in
                    my possession could perhaps stand U. S. in good stead in getting established
                    here. No aerial bombing Mukden during past 20 hours causes me believe such
                    appeal may have been made and heeded. Soonest reply requested if
                    affirmative.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Ward</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d433-f1" n="30" type="source" xml:id="d433-f1-content">
                <p>Repeated to the Ambassador in China as telegram No. 1537.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
